&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is a submission for the &lt;a href="https://dev.to/challenges/hacktoberfest-week3-2026-10-19"&gt;Hacktoberfest Open-Source AI Challenge Week 3: Slow and Steady&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What I Built
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Slow Digest turns a long group chat into two lines. Paste or export the chat, and it returns the most important change (what, when) and the most important thing you must do (who, by when). The sticker packs, match talk and goodnights are skipped.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;It is for anyone who wakes up to 200 unread messages in a class, club or project group and only needs to know what is due. You can run it from the web page, or schedule a script that writes the digest to a file while you sleep.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Demo
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Live site: &lt;a href="https://slow-digest.onrender.com" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://slow-digest.onrender.com&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The hosted site runs on Render's free plan, which has no Ollama. It uses the rule-based digest there. The open-weight model runs when you start the app on your own machine.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Code
&lt;/h2&gt;


&lt;div class="ltag-github-readme-tag"&gt;
  &lt;div class="readme-overview"&gt;
    &lt;h2&gt;
      &lt;img src="https://assets.dev.to/assets/github-logo-5a155e1f9a670af7944dd5e12375bc76ed542ea80224905ecaf878b9157cdefc.svg" alt="GitHub logo"&gt;
      &lt;a href="https://github.com/maltheshhh" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;
        maltheshhh
      &lt;/a&gt; / &lt;a href="https://github.com/maltheshhh/slow-digest" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;
        slow-digest
      &lt;/a&gt;
    &lt;/h2&gt;
    &lt;h3&gt;
      a “Sloth Summarizer” that squeezes long chats into two lines using an open-weight model that runs in your browser.
    &lt;/h3&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="ltag-github-body"&gt;

&lt;div id="readme" class="md"&gt;&lt;div class="markdown-heading"&gt;
&lt;h1 class="heading-element"&gt;Slow Digest&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A two-line morning summary of your group chat, written by an open-weight model running on your own machine.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Built for the DEV Hacktoberfest Open-Source AI Challenge, Week 3: Slow and Steady.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Paste an exported chat, get two lines: what changed, and what you must do. Jokes, stickers and goodnights are skipped.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="markdown-heading"&gt;
&lt;h2 class="heading-element"&gt;Why open&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Chats stay on your machine.&lt;/strong&gt; The server only talks to Ollama on localhost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Works offline.&lt;/strong&gt; If no model is installed, a rule-based digest takes over.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Swap the model.&lt;/strong&gt; Set &lt;code&gt;OLLAMA_MODEL&lt;/code&gt; or choose one per request.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;No cost per run.&lt;/strong&gt; No API key.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class="markdown-heading"&gt;
&lt;h2 class="heading-element"&gt;Stack&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Node 22 + Express (API and static hosting)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ollama (any open-weight model it can serve)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SQLite via the built-in &lt;code&gt;node:sqlite&lt;/code&gt; for digest history&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plain HTML, CSS and JS frontend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class="markdown-heading"&gt;
&lt;h2 class="heading-element"&gt;Run it&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight highlight-source-shell notranslate position-relative overflow-auto js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;ollama pull llama3.2:3b     &lt;span class="pl-c"&gt;&lt;span class="pl-c"&gt;#&lt;/span&gt; optional, enables the model engine&lt;/span&gt;
npm install
npm start                   &lt;span class="pl-c"&gt;&lt;span class="pl-c"&gt;#&lt;/span&gt; http://localhost:3000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Copy &lt;code&gt;.env.example&lt;/code&gt; to &lt;code&gt;.env&lt;/code&gt; and export…&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="gh-btn-container"&gt;&lt;a class="gh-btn" href="https://github.com/maltheshhh/slow-digest" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;View on GitHub&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;


  How I Built It
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Model:&lt;/strong&gt; any open-weight model that Ollama can serve. The default is &lt;code&gt;llama3.2:3b&lt;/code&gt;, and you can change it with one environment variable or per request.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Backend:&lt;/strong&gt; Node 22 and Express. &lt;code&gt;POST /api/digest&lt;/code&gt; sends the chat to Ollama on localhost and asks for exactly two lines. If Ollama is not running, the same endpoint falls back to a rule-based digest that scores messages by deadlines, days, times and numbers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;History:&lt;/strong&gt; stored in SQLite through Node's built-in &lt;code&gt;node:sqlite&lt;/code&gt;, so there are no native packages to install.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Frontend:&lt;/strong&gt; plain HTML, CSS and JS. A tiny sloth crawls along a branch while you read, at an assumed 4 metres a minute.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Overnight mode:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;code&gt;scripts/sloth_digest.py&lt;/code&gt; does the same job from the command line with the Python standard library only. Cron runs it at 3 am and the digest is in a text file by morning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Tests:&lt;/strong&gt; 5 tests cover chat parsing, the digest rules and the API.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  Why Does Open Innovation Matter?
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;A group chat holds other people's messages, so I did not want to send it to a server I do not control. With a local open-weight model, the chat never leaves the laptop.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The same choice gave me three other things a closed API would not:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;It works offline.&lt;/strong&gt; The overnight job needs only a laptop, and the app still works with no model installed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;I can swap the model.&lt;/strong&gt; A smaller one is faster, a larger one handles nuance better, and I can retune the prompt to how my friends write.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;It costs nothing per run.&lt;/strong&gt; There is no API key and no meter running while I sleep.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


  Submission Post Body:
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is a submission for the &lt;a href="https://dev.to/challenges/hacktoberfest-week3-2026-10-19"&gt;Hacktoberfest Open-Source AI Challenge Week 3: Slow and Steady&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


  What I Built
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EcoSloth AI&lt;/strong&gt; is a local-first, privacy-preserving AI assistant engineered to slow down the relentless tide of electronic waste (e-waste). &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Every year, millions of smartphones, laptops, monitors, and tablets are either tossed into municipal garbage bins or left forgotten in drawers because figuring out what to do with them feels exhausting:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Is this 6-year-old laptop worth fixing or repurposing?&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;How do I safely sign out of iCloud/Google and sanitize the storage so my data isn't exposed?&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Is this bulging battery hazardous?&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;Where can I find an authenticated, certified e-waste recycler that won't just dump toxic waste abroad?&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Instead of rushing to the trash can, &lt;strong&gt;EcoSloth AI&lt;/strong&gt; embodies the &lt;strong&gt;“Slow and Steady”&lt;/strong&gt; mindset. Users describe an unwanted electronic device (and optionally provide a photo). The local open-weight AI immediately:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Performs safety hazard triage:&lt;/strong&gt; Detects swollen lithium-ion pouch cells or high-voltage CRT internals and issues immediate physical containment instructions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Synthesizes a circular next-life pathway:&lt;/strong&gt; Prioritizes repair and creative repurposing over premature shredding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Generates non-destructive preparation checklists:&lt;/strong&gt; Walks users step-by-step through account decoupling, factory resets, and battery terminal insulation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Tracks e-waste diversions locally:&lt;/strong&gt; Records outcomes (Repaired, Reused, Donated, Resold, Recycled) in an offline SQLite database without fabricated carbon claims.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who gets to be a little lazier because of it?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
Anyone with a "junk drawer" of old electronics. Instead of spending 45 minutes searching forums, reading motherboard teardown guides, and wondering which recycling depot is legitimate, EcoSloth AI delivers an actionable triage and handoff checklist in less than 3 seconds.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;


  Demo
&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;GitHub Repository &amp;amp; Source Code:&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;a href="https://github.com/Demo-For-Test/ecosloth-ai" rel="noopener noreferrer"&gt;https://github.com/Demo-For-Test/ecosloth-ai&lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Interactive Web App:&lt;/strong&gt; Built with Streamlit (&lt;code&gt;streamlit run app.py&lt;/code&gt;) featuring an Assess Device wizard, Interactive Checklists, Local E-Waste Tracker, Verified Recycler Hub, and Multi-Format Exports (Markdown, Plain Text, and Printable HTML).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;CLI Demo Script:&lt;/strong&gt; A zero-dependency CLI script is included to test realistic triage scenarios:
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight shell"&gt;&lt;code&gt;  python demo.py
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Demo Terminal Output:&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight plaintext"&gt;&lt;code&gt;=================================================================
      [ECOSLOTH AI] LOCAL E-WASTE ASSISTANT DEMO
      'Don't throw it away. Let AI find its next life.'
=================================================================

